# {{.Project}}

An opinionated gin-kit framework application built on Gin.

## Development

```bash
go mod tidy
gin-kit run
```

The runtime lives in the versioned `github.com/Alfian57/gin-kit/framework`
dependency. Application routes, domains, services, and middleware belong in
this repository and can be customized without editing framework internals.

## Configuration

Copy `.env.example` to `.env`, then configure the database and environment.
The application loads `.env` at startup through the framework's typed
configuration: real environment variables always win over `.env` values,
malformed values fail startup, and outside development `DATABASE_URL` and
`CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` are required. Timeouts use Go duration syntax (`10s`).

Generate secrets with `openssl rand -base64 48` (for example `JWT_SECRET`).
Run `gin-kit doctor` for actionable diagnostics.

## Background work

Job handlers live in `internal/jobs` and are registered explicitly in
`app.New`. The default `QUEUE_DRIVER=sync` executes jobs inline; set
`QUEUE_DRIVER=redis` with `REDIS_URL` (the Docker Compose file ships a Redis
service) for persistent jobs with retries and a supervised worker. Add
cron-style tasks with `framework/schedule` and register the scheduler with
`application.Go("scheduler", scheduler.Run)` — single-instance per deployment.
The cache is available through `application.Cache()` (`CACHE_DRIVER=memory`
or `redis`).

## Mail and storage

Send email with `mail.New(cfg.MailOptions())` — the default `MAIL_DRIVER=log`
renders messages into the logs, and `docker compose --profile mail up` starts
Mailpit for a local inbox. Store files with
`storage.New(cfg.StorageOptions())` — `STORAGE_DRIVER=local` keeps files
under `./storage` with strict path confinement, `s3` targets any
S3-compatible store, and `docker compose --profile storage up` starts MinIO.
